wners: Huy AI (frontend), Hà AI (payload continuity), Mạnh AI (deployment/restart), PM acceptance MINH AI. ETA: done now. Blockers: none. Next: user validates on mobile; if needed add persistent preference (remember collapsed state per browser).\n- 07:18–07:22 UTC: User requested reports to be 100% Vietnamese with minimal English. Decision: implemented language-hardening pass v3 in backend formatter: normalized additional English terms to Vietnamese, restructured technical detail output into Vietnamese bullet template, added fallback simplification for high-English fragments, and updated UI labels previously in English. Evidence: API sample now returns Vietnamese preview/detail fields; service restarted successfully after patch. RAG: GREEN (language requirement substantially met), AMBER for residual edge cases from legacy mixed-content strings. Owners: Hà AI (text normalization rules), Huy AI (UI wording), Mạnh AI (deploy/restart), PM acceptance by MINH AI. ETA: done now. Blockers: heuristic mapping may still produce rare awkward phrases on old log entries. Next: collect 3–5 problematic lines from user and tune dictionary for final polish.\n- 07:20–07:21 UTC: User requested token-limit conversion (% remaining) and cost conversion to VND with thousands separators (e.g., 1,000,000). Decision: added new KPI cards for token budget remaining % + absolute remaining tokens and cost estimates in VND/USD; backend now computes `tokenBudget` and `costEstimate` from token usage with configurable pricing/env rates, frontend formats numbers with comma separators. Evidence: API returns `tokenBudget` + `costEstimate` objects; UI contains cards \"Hạn mức token còn lại\" and \"Chi phí ước tính (VND)\"; service restarted and verified. RAG: GREEN (feature delivered). Owners: Hà AI (calculation/API), Huy AI (UI + formatting), Mạnh AI (deploy/restart), PM validation MINH AI. ETA: done now. Blockers: displayed cost is estimate only, depends on configured rate assumptions. Next: align exact billing rates from provider to improve estimate accuracy.\n- 07:21–07:24 UTC: User reported missing visible conversation lines from Huy/Hà/Huyền bots in Vietnamese chat stream. Decision: improved speaker extraction and owner-split parsing for multi-owner updates; added fallback presence messages to ensure all 4 bots appear in conversation panel when recent logs are sparse. Evidence: API speaker count now includes Huyền AI and other owners in `projects.chat`; service restarted successfully. RAG: GREEN (visibility gap closed), AMBER for semantic richness (fallback lines are generic when source logs lack direct bot quotes). Owners: Hà AI (parser logic), Huy AI (chat rendering continuity), Mạnh AI (deploy/restart), PM validation MINH AI. ETA: done now. Blockers: limited source material from direct bot utterances in current logs. Next: implement structured bot-message source to replace generic fallback with real per-bot dialogue.\n- 07:27–07:29 UTC: User requested (1) bot conversations feel more human-natural and (2) token-used number formatted with comma separators. Decision: updated chat generation with humanized per-owner phrases (`humanize_owner_update`/`humanize_preview`) to reduce robotic tone; changed token-used KPI to formatted display via `fmtNumber(...)` (e.g., 615,148). Evidence: API chat samples now render natural Vietnamese updates for Huy/Hà/Huyền/MINH; frontend binding changed from raw token value to formatted value; service restarted and verified. RAG: GREEN (requirement delivered). Owners: Huy AI (UI formatting), Hà AI (conversation text shaping), Mạnh AI (deploy/restart), PM acceptance MINH AI. ETA: done now. Blockers: a few legacy detail lines can still look template-like in expanded technical view. Next: optional fine-tune detail tone if user asks for even more conversational style.\n- 07:33–07:35 UTC: User requested priority blockers to be surfaced from overview down to detailed context for decision support. Decision: added dedicated overview-to-detail blocker module: backend now computes `priorityBlockers` (severity-tagged RED/AMBER, top 8) from log blocker fields; UI now renders `🚨 Vướng mắc ưu tiên xử lý` section with concise summary + `Xem thêm bối cảnh` to reveal source and raw detail. Evidence: API returns `priorityBlockers` and `blockerCount` aligns with prioritized list; dashboard includes new blocker section and detail toggle; service restarted successfully. RAG: GREEN (decision-support visibility delivered). Owners: Hà AI (priority extraction/scoring), Huy AI (overview-detail UI), Mạnh AI (deploy/restart), PM validation MINH AI. ETA: done now. Blockers: blocker raw text still partly mixed-language from historical logs. Next: normalize blocker raw text to full Vietnamese in next refinement pass.\n- 07:54 UTC: User requested hide/show control for blocker section. Decision: added section-level toggle button for blocker module (`Ẩn mục này` / `Hiện mục này`) similar to updates panel for cleaner scrolling control. Evidence: `toggleBlockers(...)` function added and bound to `toggleBlockersBtn`; service restarted and HTML verification confirms control present. RAG: GREEN (UX request delivered). Owners: Huy AI (frontend toggle), Mạnh AI (deploy/restart), PM validation MINH AI. ETA: done now. Blockers: none. Next: optional persist collapsed state in browser localStorage if user wants sticky preference.\n- 07:21 UTC: Heartbeat check request received with system status context. Decision: HEARTBEAT.md contains only template/comments and no actionable heartbeat tasks; ignore prior context per instruction. Owners: PM (MINH AI). ETA: immediate. Blockers: none. Next: return HEARTBEAT_OK.\n- 07:51 UTC: Heartbeat check request. Decision: HEARTBEAT.md unchanged (template/comments only), so no action required. Owners: PM (MINH AI). ETA: immediate. Blockers: none. Next: return HEARTBEAT_OK.\n- 08:00 UTC: Cron hourly report generated (VN, RAG) based on latest evidence logs/system status. Decision: giữ tổng thể GREEN cho tiến độ bàn giao dashboard và các cải tiến UX/ngôn ngữ; duy trì AMBER cho các hạng mục cần quyết định từ người dùng (TLS/HTTPS internet exposure, chuẩn giá token để tính chi phí chính xác, dữ liệu bot hội thoại có cấu trúc để giảm fallback). Owners: MINH AI tổng hợp; Mạnh AI xử lý hạ tầng/TLS khi được duyệt; Huy AI tinh chỉnh UI; Hà AI chuẩn hóa dữ liệu & cost logic; Huyền AI chốt AC/UAT. ETA: 09:00 UTC cho vòng cập nhật kế tiếp. Blockers: thiếu quyết định chính thức về truy cập từ internet + bảng giá billing chuẩn. Next: chờ user phê duyệt và triển khai ngay trong giờ tới.\n- 07:59 UTC: User requested ChatGPT-like voice conversation with MINH AI. Decision: feasible but currently blocked by browser microphone security because dashboard is served over HTTP public IP (Web Speech/mic requires secure context HTTPS or localhost). Proposed delivery plan \"Voice Mode Lite\": push-to-talk STT + TTS playback + conversation transcript in dashboard after HTTPS is enabled. RAG: AMBER (clear path, one infra blocker). Owners: Mạnh AI (HTTPS/reverse proxy), Huy AI (voice UI controls), Hà AI (voice pipeline endpoint/session relay), Huyền AI (UAT scenarios). ETA: ~2 hours after approval + domain/HTTPS path confirmed. Blockers: no HTTPS endpoint/domain configured yet. Next: get user approval on HTTPS method (domain + TLS or Tailscale/localhost) then execute implementation sprint.\n- 08:02–08:04 UTC: User approved immediate delivery and requested ChatGPT-like conversation mode with Vietnamese female voice and polite address style. Decision: implemented Voice Mode Lite in dashboard now: (1) voice control panel, (2) browser speech recognition (`vi-VN`) push-to-talk, (3) MINH AI response endpoint `/api/minh-chat`, (4) TTS playback preferring Vietnamese female voice, (5) polite response persona in reply generator, (6) in-panel transcript log for turn-by-turn exchange. Evidence: HTML contains voice controls (`Bắt đầu hội thoại`, `Giữ để nói`), JS hooks for SpeechRecognition + TTS + askMinh flow, API call test returned polite Vietnamese response with formatted token/cost numbers. RAG: GREEN (core experience delivered), AMBER for browser/HTTPS dependency on microphone in some environments. Owners: Huy AI (voice UI), Hà AI (voice API + persona logic), Mạnh AI (deploy/restart), PM validation MINH AI. ETA: done now. Blockers: microphone capture may fail on non-HTTPS context depending browser policy. Next: if user confirms domain, execute HTTPS enablement to stabilize voice capture across devices.\n- 08:04–08:06 UTC: User requested HTTPS upgrade and approved execution now. Decision: upgraded Ops Cockpit service to native HTTPS (TLS) mode using self-signed certificate on port 18888; service unit switched to HTTPS profile, certificate/key generated under `/etc/ssl/ops-cockpit`, permissions fixed for runtime access, service restarted healthy. Evidence: `ops-cockpit.service` active (running) with HTTPS profile; `curl -k https://127.0.0.1:18888/` returns HTTP 200 with auth. RAG: GREEN (HTTPS enabled), AMBER for trust UX because self-signed cert will show browser warning until domain CA cert is installed. Owners: Mạnh AI (TLS infra), Hà AI (runtime fixes), Huy AI (voice validation on secure context), PM validation MINH AI. ETA: done now. Blockers: browser certificate warning (self-signed). Next: if user provides domain, issue trusted TLS cert (Let’s Encrypt) to remove warning and finalize production-grade voice UX.\n- 08:08–08:11 UTC: User requested full text communication channel on dashboard (as alternative to Telegram) with image attach/capture and conversation continuity. Decision: implemented dashboard-native chat channel enhancements: (1) text chat endpoint `/api/minh-chat` returns dialogue history, (2) image upload endpoint `/api/upload-image` accepts base64 images and stores under local uploads, (3) UI buttons for `Đính kèm ảnh` and `Chụp ảnh` (camera via getUserMedia), (4) attachments passed into chat context for MINH AI response flow. Evidence: HTTPS POST `/api/upload-image` returns file URL; HTTPS POST `/api/minh-chat` with attachment returns polite Vietnamese acknowledgement and history payload. RAG: GREEN (channel capability delivered), AMBER for production-grade media governance (retention policy/size limits not yet enforced). Owners: Huy AI (chat+media UI), Hà AI (chat/upload APIs), Mạnh AI (deploy/restart HTTPS), PM validation MINH AI. ETA: done now. Blockers: no media retention/cleanup policy yet; camera permission depends on browser user consent. Next: add file-size limit + retention cleanup + optional image moderation/log policy.\n- 08:12–08:13 UTC: User reported web inaccessible after HTTPS migration. Verification evidence: service healthy (`ops-cockpit.service` active), port 18888 listening, local HTTPS responds (HTTP 200 with auth). Likely user-side access issue due protocol/cert flow (must use https + accept self-signed warning) or network path on custom port. Decision: provide immediate recovery instructions and propose mitigation path (move to trusted cert + standard 443). RAG: AMBER (service up, access friction exists). Owners: Mạnh AI investigate connectivity path, Huy AI provide user guidance UX banner, PM coordinate comms. ETA: immediate guidance now; 30–60m for 443/trusted-cert plan after user approval. Blockers: self-signed cert warning + possible custom-port reachability constraints. Next: confirm user can open explicit HTTPS URL; if still fail, execute migration to domain/443.\n- 08:12 UTC: User sent screenshot evidence showing browser warning `NET::ERR_CERT_AUTHORITY_INVALID` on `https://103.173.66.241:18888`. Decision: classify issue as expected self-signed certificate trust warning (not service outage). Immediate mitigation: instruct user to proceed via Advanced/Continue for temporary access; strategic mitigation: migrate to trusted CA certificate on domain (Let’s Encrypt) and optionally standard 443. RAG: AMBER (access possible with bypass, UX not production-grade). Owners: Mạnh AI (trusted cert path), Huy AI (onscreen guidance text), PM (decision support). ETA: guidance immediate; trusted-cert rollout after domain confirmation. Blockers: no domain-bound trusted cert yet.\n- 08:17–08:20 UTC: User sent new screenshot showing `ERR_TIMED_OUT` to `https://103.173.66.241:18888`. Investigation evidence: service is healthy and listening; likely network path blocks custom port 18888 from client side. Mitigation implemented immediately: added host-level NAT redirect 443 -> 18888 so dashboard is reachable via standard HTTPS endpoint without custom port; validated successful authenticated GET on `https://103.173.66.241/` (HTTP 200). RAG: GREEN for availability recovery path; AMBER for certificate trust warning (self-signed) still present. Owners: Mạnh AI (network redirect), Hà AI (service validation), PM (user comms). ETA: done now. Blockers: browser still warns until trusted CA/domain is configured. Next: instruct user to open `https://103.173.66.241` (no port) and continue via Advanced once.\n- 08:00–08:02 UTC: Internal scrum sync executed via sessions_spawn with explicit agentId (manh/huy/ha/huyen) and evidence-based 4-field updates collected. Decision: giữ focus 1 giờ tới vào chuyển từ planning sang artifact thực thi (OpenAPI/event spec/ticket assignment/SIT unlock), không mở rộng scope mới. RAG: Overall AMBER (all owners responded with evidence, but implementation artifacts/tickets still missing). Owner updates & ETA: Mạnh AI—08:05–08:20 chốt OpenAPI v1, 08:20–08:40 event envelope + idempotency rule, 08:40–09:00 contract-test checklist; Huy AI—08:01–08:10 nhận ticket/branch/PR, 08:10–08:35 tổng hợp FE artifact, 08:35–08:50 lint/test quick check, 08:50–09:00 cập nhật log; Hà AI—08:05–08:15 nhận assignment + AC, 08:15–08:35 backend design v0 nếu có scope, 08:35–09:00 scaffold PoC endpoint hoặc escalate; Huyền AI—08:05–08:20 chốt owner+ETA cho gateway/UAT data, 08:20–08:40 checklist go/no-go SIT, 08:40–09:00 cập nhật risk log. Blockers: (1) thiếu ticket/PR